unit: pc-split-deploy-honesty
commits: 33fe8ac8c (adopt_served / push_router_aliases extracted, behaviour-preserving),
  c09c05eb8 (a reload serve did not honour is refused, naming each slot),
  a0a241d45 (svrn follows serve's self-report across a serve restart),
  bf406e8c3 (the mesh-status bullet has no site after the flip; premise corrected)
what: on the dialing path `POST /v1/admin/reload` succeeds only when serve's
  self-report holds the core slots `[models]` asks for, and otherwise names
  each one; svrn re-reads serve's self-report every 10 s and adopts a changed
  one, so a serve restart reaches `/v1/models`, `/status` and the manifest.
  `/v1/mesh/status` is cw-rails' and reads no serve state, so the third
  bullet has no site. Decision: ralph/decisions/phase-c-8.md.
